# {{projectName}}

An Apache Airflow deployment scaffolded with **dude** (`airflow` stack):
Airflow 3 running in Docker Compose locally{{#if withIac}}, and on AWS ECS
Fargate (Terraform, ECS executor) in the cloud{{/if}}, with an organized,
lint-enforced layout for DAGs, plugins, packages and configuration.

## Quickstart

```bash
{{#if withEntraId}}
# 1. fill AZURE_TENANT_ID / AZURE_CLIENT_ID / AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET in .env
#    (see the SSO page for the Entra ID app registration)
{{/if}}
dude up --build          # build the image + start every component
open http://localhost:8080
{{#unless withEntraId}}
# sign in with admin / admin (change it in .env)
{{/unless}}
```

The example DAGs under `airflow/dags/examples/` arrive **paused** — unpause
them in the UI (or `dude dag trigger --id example_etl`).

## What's inside

| Path | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| `airflow/dags/` | DAG definitions — one DAG per file, `examples/` to learn from, `lib/` for shared helpers |
| `airflow/plugins/ops_toolkit/` | Reference plugin: listeners + macros + a custom timetable |
| `airflow/requirements.txt` | Python packages baked into the image (pinned) |
| `airflow/config/webserver_config.py` | Sign-on configuration ({{#if withEntraId}}Microsoft Entra ID{{else}}native user DB{{/if}}) |
| `airflow/tests/` | DAG integrity suite (`dude test`) |
| `.env` / `.env.example` | Environment variables & local secrets — the deployment contract |
{{#if withIac}}
| `iac/` | Terraform for AWS ECS Fargate (see *Deploy*) |
{{/if}}
| `.claude/rules/AF/` | The project conventions, one page per `dude lint` rule |

## Daily commands

```bash
dude up / dude down      # start / stop the deployment
dude logs [service]      # follow logs
dude dag list            # what's deployed
dude dag errors          # import errors, if any
dude lint                # structural conventions (AF rules)
dude test                # DAG integrity suite (runs in the image)
dude format              # ruff format + import sort
dude docs                # this documentation, live-reloading
```

See *Project guide* for how to add DAGs, packages, plugins, and environment
variables — and *Command reference* for everything `dude` can do here.
